<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<PermissionSet xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        AllowViewEditConvertedLeads ADDED 2026-08-17 (business requirement: every Lead must be
        visible to the acquisition team). Confirmed by measurement: after
        sharingRules/Lead.sharingRules-meta.xml's new Lead_Acquisition_Team_All rule was live,
        UserRecordAccess for both Junior Dhanani and Nikhil Dhanani against non-converted Leads
        showed correct Edit/Read access, but against every CONVERTED Lead sampled (13 of 42
        live Leads in this org) returned ZERO rows for both users - not even an explicit
        HasReadAccess=false row. This is a Salesforce platform gate independent of sharing and
        object CRUD: a converted Lead is invisible to a user who lacks this userPermission,
        regardless of any sharing rule or Edit/Read grant on Lead. No permission set in this
        repo granted it before this change (grepped force-app/main/default/permissionsets/).

        WHY DPEG_Base_Access (layer 1) AND NOT A MODULE SET. This is the one permission set
        common to BOTH DPEG_Junior_Analyst_PSG and DPEG_Principal_PSG (see their
        permissionsetgroup-meta.xml files) - the requirement is for the whole acquisition team,
        not one persona, and this is a platform userPermissions grant, which is layer 1's exact
        contract per ARCHITECTURE.md's seven-layer permission set model.
    -->
    <description>Grants Lightning Experience User so every DPEG team member logs into Lightning, not Classic. Also grants View and Edit Converted Leads, without which a converted Lead is invisible regardless of sharing/CRUD (2026-08-17).</description>
    <hasActivationRequired>false</hasActivationRequired>
    <label>DPEG Base Access</label>
    <userPermissions>
        <enabled>true</enabled>
        <name>LightningExperienceUser</name>
    </userPermissions>
    <userPermissions>
        <enabled>true</enabled>
        <name>AllowViewEditConvertedLeads</name>
    </userPermissions>
</PermissionSet>
